    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104157" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοί</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταί,</span>
		
			Ep.
		 and poet. for οἱ or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἵ, αἱ</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἵ,</span> nom. pl. of ὁ and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅ,</span> freq. in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> (relat., <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			3.73
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			12.63
		</span></i>, more freq. demonstr.), not in 
			Ion.
		 Prose, rare in Trag., e.g. <i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Pers.</u>
			424
		</span></i>: but in 
			Dor.
		 and certain other dialects as the Article, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἱάρων . . καὶ τοὶ Συρακόσιοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					35
				</span></i>
			<u>Ba</u> (Olympia, V B.C.), etc.</div>
